nes, -2 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 2, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "build-with-claude/files", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+6 lines, -12 lines", "added": 6, "removed": 12, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "build-with-claude/claude-on-amazon-bedrock", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+1 lines, -1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 1, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "agents-and-tools/tool-use/overview", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+2 lines, -5 lines", "added": 2, "removed": 5, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "agents-and-tools/tool-use/computer-use-tool", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+16 lines, -16 lines", "added": 16, "removed": 16, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "agents-and-tools/tool-use/web-fetch-tool", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+27 lines, -3 lines", "added": 27, "removed": 3, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "agents-and-tools/tool-use/memory-tool", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "+1 lines, -1 lines", "added": 1, "removed": 1, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "agents-and-tools/mcp-connector", "source_id": "anthropic-api", "source_name": "Anthropic API", "summary": "Formatting changes", "added": 0, "removed": 0, "analysis": null}], "analysis": "## \u6587\u6863\u53d8\u66f4\u6279\u91cf\u5206\u6790\n\n### 1. \u603b\u4f53\u6982\u8981\n\n\u672c\u6b21\u53d8\u66f4\u6d89\u53ca\u672f\u8bed\u5927\u89c4\u6a21\u91cd\u547d\u540d\uff08\"Routines\" \u2192 \"Cloud scheduled tasks\"\u3001\"scheduled tasks\" \u2192 \"session-scoped scheduled tasks\"\uff09\uff0c\u65b0\u589e `between_tools` \u601d\u8003\u6a21\u5f0f API \u80fd\u529b\u58f0\u660e\uff0c\u5b8c\u5584\u4e86 `CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` \u73af\u5883\u53d8\u91cf\u7684\u6821\u9a8c/\u8b66\u544a\u6587\u6863\uff0c\u4ee5\u53ca\u6f84\u6e05\u4e86 `dontAsk` \u6743\u9650\u6a21\u5f0f\u4e0b mods \u7684\u5ba1\u6279\u884c\u4e3a\u3002\u540c\u65f6\u5c06 API \u8ba4\u8bc1\u5934\u4ece `x-api-key` \u6539\u4e3a `Authorization: Bearer`\u3002\n\n### 2. \u5173\u952e\u4e3b\u9898\n\n- **\u672f\u8bed\u91cd\u547d\u540d**\uff1a\"Routines\" \u5168\u9762\u66f4\u540d\u4e3a \"Cloud scheduled tasks\"\uff0c\u539f \"scheduled tasks\"\uff08`/loop`\uff09\u66f4\u540d\u4e3a \"session-scoped scheduled tasks\"\uff0c\u4e09\u8005\u5f62\u6210\u6e05\u6670\u7684\u547d\u540d\u4f53\u7cfb\uff1acloud scheduled tasks / desktop scheduled tasks / session-scoped scheduled tasks\n- **\u65b0\u601d\u8003\u6a21\u5f0f `between_tools`**\uff1aModels API \u65b0\u589e `thinking.types.between_tools` \u80fd\u529b\u5b57\u6bb5\uff0c\u8868\u793a\u5173\u95ed\u524d\u7f6e\u601d\u8003\u4f46\u4fdd\u7559\u5de5\u5177\u8c03\u7528\u95f4\u7684\u8fdb\u5ea6\u66f4\u65b0\n- **`CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` \u5b8c\u5584**\uff1a\u65b0\u589e\u8be6\u7ec6\u7684\u8b66\u544a\u8bed\u4e49\u8868\u3001\u6709\u6548\u503c\u8303\u56f4\u8bf4\u660e\uff0cv2.1.304+ \u652f\u6301 `k`/`M` \u540e\u7f00\uff1b\u660e\u786e\u8be5\u53d8\u91cf\u8bbe\u7f6e\u540e `used_percentage` \u4e0d\u518d\u53cd\u6620\u538b\u7f29\u89e6\u53d1\u65f6\u673a\n- **\u6743\u9650\u6a21\u578b\u6f84\u6e05**\uff1a`dontAsk` \u6a21\u5f0f\u4e0b\u5df2\u5b89\u88c5\u7684 mod \u4ecd\u53ef\u6279\u51c6\u90e8\u5206\u88ab hook \u963b\u6b62\u7684\u8c03\u7528\uff0c\u4f46\u53d7\u9650\u4e8e\u65e0\u6258\u7ba1\u8bbe\u7f6e\u4e14\u672a\u4f7f\u7528 Team/Enterprise \u767b\u5f55\u51ed\u636e\n- **API \u8ba4\u8bc1\u5934\u66f4\u65b0**\uff1a\u793a\u4f8b\u4ece `x-api-key` \u8fc1\u79fb\u81f3 `Authorization: Bearer` \u6807\u51c6\u683c\u5f0f\n- **\u4ee3\u7801\u793a\u4f8b\u98ce\u683c\u7edf\u4e00**\uff1a\u591a\u5904\u79fb\u9664\u5c3e\u9017\u53f7\u3001\u7b80\u5316 TypeScript \u7c7b\u578b\u65ad\u8a00\u4e3a\u666e\u901a\u56de\u8c03\n\n### 3. \u5f71\u54cd\u7b49\u7ea7\uff1a**Medium**\n\n\u672f\u8bed\u91cd\u547d\u540d\u4e0d\u7834\u574f\u529f\u80fd\uff08URL \u548c\u914d\u7f6e\u8def\u5f84\u4e0d\u53d8\uff09\uff0c\u4f46\u5f00\u53d1\u8005\u9700\u66f4\u65b0\u5fc3\u667a\u6a21\u578b\u548c\u5185\u90e8\u6587\u6863\u5f15\u7528\u3002`between_tools` \u601d\u8003\u6a21\u5f0f\u548c API \u8ba4\u8bc1\u5934\u53d8\u66f4\u662f\u65b0\u589e/\u6807\u51c6\u5316\u7684 API \u884c\u4e3a\uff0c\u9700\u5173\u6ce8\u4f46\u4e0d\u7834\u574f\u73b0\u6709\u8c03\u7528\u3002`CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` \u7684\u6821\u9a8c\u884c\u4e3a\u53d8\u66f4\u53ef\u80fd\u5f71\u54cd\u5df2\u6709\u811a\u672c\u4e2d\u7684\u65e0\u6548\u503c\uff08\u4e4b\u524d\u9759\u9ed8\u5ffd\u7565\uff0c\u73b0\u5728\u4f1a\u8b66\u544a\u5e76\u91c7\u7528\u56de\u9000\u503c\uff09\u3002\n\n### 4. \u5f00\u53d1\u8005\u884c\u52a8\u9879\n\n- **\u66f4\u65b0\u672f\u8bed\u8ba4\u77e5**\uff1a\u5c06\"routines\"\u66ff\u6362\u4e3a\"cloud scheduled tasks\"\uff0c\u533a\u5206 cloud / desktop / session-scoped \u4e09\u7c7b\u5b9a\u65f6\u4efb\u52a1\uff0c\u907f\u514d\u5728\u56e2\u961f\u6c9f\u901a\u548c\u81ea\u52a8\u5316\u811a\u672c\u6ce8\u91ca\u4e2d\u6df7\u6dc6\n- **\u68c0\u67e5 `CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` \u811a\u672c**\uff1a\u5982\u679c\u811a\u672c\u4e2d\u8bbe\u7f6e\u4e86\u8be5\u53d8\u91cf\uff0c\u786e\u8ba4\u503c\u5728 100,000\u20131,000,000 \u8303\u56f4\u5185\uff1b\u6ce8\u610f\u88f8\u6570\u5b57\u542b\u4e49\uff08`200` = 200 tokens\uff0c\u800c\u975e 200K\uff09\uff1bv2.1.304+ \u53ef\u7528 `200k`/`1M` \u540e\u7f00\n- **\u8bc4\u4f30 `between_tools` \u601d\u8003\u6a21\u5f0f**\uff1a\u5982\u9700\u5173\u95ed\u524d\u7f6e\u601d\u8003\u4f46\u4fdd\u7559\u5de5\u5177\u95f4\u63a8\u7406\uff0c\u53ef\u5728 Models API \u4e2d\u67e5\u8be2 `thinking.types.between_tools.supported` \u540e\u4f7f\u7528 `thinking: {type: \"between_tools\"}`\n- **\u5ba1\u67e5 `dontAsk` + mods \u7ec4\u5408**\uff1a\u82e5\u4f9d\u8d56 `dontAsk` \u505a\u4e25\u683c CI \u9501\u5b9a\uff0c\u6ce8\u610f\u5df2\u5b89\u88c5\u7684 mod \u53ef\u7ed5\u8fc7 hook \u7684 deny \u51b3\u7b56\uff08\u9664\u975e\u6709\u6258\u7ba1\u8bbe\u7f6e\u6216 Team/Enterprise \u767b\u5f55\uff09\n- **\u8fc1\u79fb API \u8ba4\u8bc1\u5934**\uff1a\u5c06\u793a\u4f8b\u4e2d\u7684 `x-api-key` \u5934\u66ff\u6362\u4e3a `Authorization: Bearer` \u6807\u51c6\u683c\u5f0f", "reasoning": "Let me analyze this batch of documentation changes across 32 pages.\n\nKey changes I'm seeing:\n\n1. **\"Routines\" renamed to \"Cloud scheduled tasks\"** - This is a major terminology change across many pages (claude-code-on-the-web.md, common-workflows.md, overview.md, skills.md, slash-commands.md, interactive-mode.md, hooks.md, costs.md, sub-agents.md). The term \"routines\" is being replaced with \"cloud scheduled tasks\" to better distinguish from \"desktop scheduled tasks\" and \"session-scoped scheduled tasks\" (/loop).\n\n2. **\"Scheduled tasks\" clarified as \"session-scoped scheduled tasks\"** - In costs.md, hooks.md, skills.md, slash-commands.md - the term \"scheduled task\" is being qualified as \"session-scoped scheduled task\" to distinguish from cloud scheduled tasks and desktop scheduled tasks.\n\n3. **`CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` values and warnings** - model-config.md adds detailed documentation about warning messages, valid values, and behavior when the value is out of range. Also adds support for `k` and `M` suffixes in the env var (v2.1.304+). sub-agents.md also gets a cross-reference.\n\n4. **`dontAsk` permission mode and mods interaction** - headless.md and hooks-guide.md clarify that mods can approve calls that `dontAsk` would otherwise deny. hooks-guide.md adds a Note with conditions under which a mod can override a hook's block (no managed settings, no Team/Enterprise login).\n\n5. **`thinking.types.between_tools` capability** - about-claude/models/overview.md and api/models/list.md add documentation for a new thinking type `between_tools` which turns off up-front thinking but allows progress updates between tool calls.\n\n6. **API authentication header change** - api/beta-headers.md changes from `x-api-key: YOUR_API_KEY` to `Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY`.\n\n7. **Code style changes** - Multiple pages (extended-thinking.md, prompt-caching.md, citations.md, search-results.md, structured-outputs.md, effort.md) have trailing comma removals and type assertion simplifications in code examples.\n\n8. **Structured outputs on Bedrock** - structured-outputs.md removes the legacy Bedrock note, now just shows \"ga\" for Amazon Bedrock.\n\n9. **Batch processing** - batch-processing.md clarifies that workspaces and billing are \"in the Claude Console\".\n\n10. **API overview** - Minor wording change about viewing rate limits.\n\n11. **IP allowlist section restructured** - claude-code-on-the-web.md breaks the IP allowlist bullet into sub-bullets for better readability.\n\nLet me assess impact:\n- The terminology change from \"routines\" to \"cloud scheduled tasks\" is significant but not breaking - it's a naming change, the underlying feature/URL remains the same\n- The `between_tools` thinking type is new API capability\n- The auth header change from `x-api-key` to `Authorization: Bearer` could be significant for API users\n- The `CLAUDE_CODE_AUTO_COMPACT_WINDOW` warnings documentation is important for ops\n- The mods/dontAsk clarification affects permission model understanding"}, {"timestamp": "14:15 EST", "sources": [{"id": "claude-code", "name": "Claude Code", "pages": [{"slug": "amazon-bedrock", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+16 lines, -76 lines", "added": 16, "removed": 76, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "analytics", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+16 lines, -20 lines", "added": 16, "removed": 20, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "checkpointing", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+4 lines, -4 lines", "added": 4, "removed": 4, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "chrome", "source_id": "claude-code", "source_name": "Claude Code", "summary": "+18 lines, -24 lines", "added": 18, "removed": 24, "analysis": null}, {"slug": "claude-code-on-the-web", "source_id": "claude-code", "source